    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0853" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg771"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 677.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 10, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit a copy of a report of Major
                    General Oanby, and of the accompanying papers, relative to certain proceedings
                    near Brownsville, in Texas, in connexion with the United States, Texan, and
                    French forces in that quarter. The condition of affairs there does not seem to
                    have been changed, but these papers will serve to explain it. To that end you
                    may communicate them to M. Drouyn de Lhuys.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>













